WEBVTT

00:00:29.125 --> 00:00:31.167
Good morning,
ladies and gentlemen.

00:00:31.167 --> 00:00:33.792
My name is Sugata Eishiro.

00:00:36.542 --> 00:00:39.208
This is my assistant,

00:00:39.208 --> 00:00:40.917
Pretty II.

00:00:42.875 --> 00:00:47.042
515 years ago, in 1494,

00:00:47.042 --> 00:00:50.708
Portugal and Spain signed
the Treaty of Tordesillas,

00:00:50.708 --> 00:00:55.333
and then in 1529,
they signed the Treaty of Saragossa.

00:00:55.333 --> 00:00:58.292
The world was divided by
these two great powers longitudinally,

00:00:58.292 --> 00:01:00.542
much like the lines on a watermelon.

00:01:00.542 --> 00:01:03.500
This came to be known as <i>demarcació</i>n.

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:08.500
This watermelon could be
said to represent the New World--

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:12.208
which is to say, the world newly
divided by this <i>demarcació</i>n.

00:01:13.042 --> 00:01:15.167
It is within these old notions

00:01:15.167 --> 00:01:18.625
that hints to the new world must be hidden.

00:01:23.167 --> 00:01:25.833
"New World"

00:01:27.208 --> 00:01:30.083
Dismiss not the watermelon.

00:01:31.708 --> 00:01:36.875
"Grave of Pretty I"

00:01:36.917 --> 00:01:39.958
<i>I can hear my heart bell</i>

00:01:39.958 --> 00:01:42.542
<i>dou shita tte iu no</i>

00:01:42.542 --> 00:01:46.250
<i>mune no beru ga naru</i>

00:01:47.625 --> 00:01:51.958
"Heaven's Lost Property"

00:01:52.042 --> 00:01:57.792
<i>hajimari wa ano toki datta (ringin' ringin')</i>

00:01:57.792 --> 00:02:03.542
<i>kimi ga me no mae ni totsuzen (ringin' ringin')</i>

00:02:03.542 --> 00:02:08.708
<i>arawareta no wa umareru mae kara</i>

00:02:08.708 --> 00:02:11.625
<i>kimerarete'ta n da ne</i>

00:02:11.625 --> 00:02:14.542
<i>kitto sou da yo</i>

00:02:14.542 --> 00:02:20.042
<i>negai ya yabou ya kuusou ga</i>

00:02:20.042 --> 00:02:25.750
<i>shiranai reberu e doa o tataite</i>

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:31.958
<i>habataku kagi to mirai o kureru</i>
<i>(with your wings)</i>

00:02:31.958 --> 00:02:34.875
<i>I can hear my heart bell</i>

00:02:34.875 --> 00:02:37.917
<i>tomerarenai yo</i>

00:02:37.917 --> 00:02:43.583
<i>tenshi ga narashiteru</i>
<i>"daisuki" no aizu da yo ne</i>

00:02:43.583 --> 00:02:46.458
<i>can you hear my heart bell?</i>

00:02:46.458 --> 00:02:48.792
<i>dou shita tte iu no</i>

00:02:48.792 --> 00:02:54.208
<i>kiita koto ga nai mune no beru ga naru</i>

00:02:54.208 --> 00:03:03.333
<i>sore de mo mada kimi</i>
<i>wa nani mo shiranai keredo</i>

00:03:08.042 --> 00:03:10.500
Ah, this is aggravating!

00:03:11.458 --> 00:03:12.542
What's wrong?

00:03:12.542 --> 00:03:16.333
Look at this math
homework from Takehara.

00:03:16.333 --> 00:03:21.333
He always gives out homework that
no ordinary person can do!

00:03:22.958 --> 00:03:25.917
If that's how he wants it,
I'll solve these problems, no matter what!

00:03:25.917 --> 00:03:28.083
Way to go, Tomo!

00:03:28.083 --> 00:03:32.250
But I can't even understand what
these questions mean.

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:33.792
Tomo, do you?

00:03:33.792 --> 00:03:36.417
That's crazy. Sohara, if you can't solve these,

00:03:36.417 --> 00:03:39.208
then they're obviously too much for me!

00:03:40.458 --> 00:03:42.750
Ah, what a pain.

00:03:48.583 --> 00:03:52.125
I know. I'll have Ikaros
produce some other card, and...

00:03:52.125 --> 00:03:55.708
No way! We'll have real problems
if anything else strange happens!

00:03:56.958 --> 00:03:59.417
Sheesh, well <i>I </i>thought it
was a good idea.

00:03:59.417 --> 00:04:02.500
You'll have to do it on the level.
What choice do you have?

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:06.333
And you're not going to finish
your homework lying on the floor.

00:04:15.375 --> 00:04:18.542
Are you listening to me? Tomo?

00:04:22.042 --> 00:04:25.292
Um, Sohara, the area of the triangle

00:04:25.292 --> 00:04:29.292
formed by your white polka-dots
is the base times the height--

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:40.458
Geez, we'll never get our
homework done like this, will we?

00:04:40.458 --> 00:04:45.042
I know! Sugata might
be able to teach us this math.

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:49.042
"Angeloid Directive Zero"

00:04:49.167 --> 00:04:49.792
"Sugata"

00:04:49.792 --> 00:04:51.875
This is indeed
the Sugata household,

00:04:51.875 --> 00:04:54.458
but there are no children
here named Eishiro.

00:04:55.333 --> 00:04:57.083
That's strange.

00:04:57.083 --> 00:05:00.917
This is the only house in
the area with Sugatas living in it.

00:05:00.917 --> 00:05:04.125
I can't reach him on his cell
phone, either. What do we do?

00:05:04.125 --> 00:05:06.750
Oh, well if it isn't Mitsuki.

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:09.208
Ah, Chairman!

00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:11.667
Hi there, Student Council Chairman.

00:05:11.667 --> 00:05:13.208
Off on a date today?

00:05:13.208 --> 00:05:14.417
No, we're not!

00:05:14.417 --> 00:05:19.250
Oh, no? You two are still close
enough that you share baths, right?

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:20.625
We are not!

00:05:20.625 --> 00:05:23.375
Sakurai, is it true what I heard

00:05:23.375 --> 00:05:27.333
about you choosing all of
Mitsuki's underwear?

00:05:27.333 --> 00:05:29.792
N-No, it's not.

00:05:29.792 --> 00:05:34.708
Earlier, you had Mitsuki
handcuffed with her panties off, huh?

00:05:34.708 --> 00:05:37.708
W-Well, that was...

00:05:38.958 --> 00:05:42.458
By the way, it looks like you're
looking for Sugata's house.

00:05:42.458 --> 00:05:45.750
If you know that, then please
don't zing us with your little skit!

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:50.333
Head down to the riverbed.
Would you like me to show you the way?

00:05:51.583 --> 00:05:53.417
The riverbed?

00:06:02.167 --> 00:06:02.792
"Sugata"

00:06:02.792 --> 00:06:04.083
Your house?!

00:06:04.083 --> 00:06:06.250
<i>This </i>is your house?!

00:06:06.250 --> 00:06:08.250
Hmm? Yes, that's right.

00:06:08.875 --> 00:06:12.833
Sugata, don't tell me you
come to school from here every day!

00:06:12.833 --> 00:06:16.667
Indeed I do. Welcome to my home.

00:06:16.667 --> 00:06:18.333
Thank you for having us.

00:06:18.333 --> 00:06:20.625
Not at all. My pleasure.

00:06:22.667 --> 00:06:26.042
As for question 3, part 1, for the identity

00:06:26.042 --> 00:06:34.208
(cosθ + i sinθ)5 = cos5θ;
we expand the left side.

00:06:34.208 --> 00:06:36.250
When we do, the left side equals...

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:38.667
Quite the low-level problem, huh?

00:06:38.667 --> 00:06:41.250
Yeah. If he's going to
play at being a mathematician,

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:44.333
I wish he'd come up
with some tougher problems.

00:06:44.333 --> 00:06:48.500
Awesome. They're way over our level.

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:54.875
Is something the matter?

00:06:54.875 --> 00:06:55.958
Hey!

00:06:55.958 --> 00:06:59.750
Ikaros, would you like
to try taking it from here?

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:02.042
Who, me?

00:07:10.042 --> 00:07:12.750
Sugata, why ask Ikaros?

00:07:12.750 --> 00:07:17.375
Tomoki, you mentioned that
she called herself a "product," right?

00:07:17.375 --> 00:07:23.292
I am a product of Synapse,
created only to please my master.

00:07:23.292 --> 00:07:25.417
Yes, that's what she said.

00:07:25.417 --> 00:07:28.750
So then, assuming that she is like a robot,

00:07:28.750 --> 00:07:32.458
I was thinking that she might
have excellent computational abilities.

00:07:32.458 --> 00:07:33.667
I am finished.

00:07:33.667 --> 00:07:34.750
That was fast!

00:07:34.750 --> 00:07:36.000
Awesome!

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:40.833
Well now, we didn't have to come
all the way over to Sugata's, did we?

00:07:41.375 --> 00:07:44.750
"Master"

00:07:47.292 --> 00:07:49.458
Well, shall we continue?

00:07:49.458 --> 00:07:51.167
If you wouldn't mind.

00:07:51.167 --> 00:07:53.375
Man, you got my hopes up!

00:07:53.375 --> 00:07:56.125
What's worse, you wrote it
in pen! I can't erase it!

00:07:56.125 --> 00:07:57.292
My homework!

00:07:57.292 --> 00:07:59.792
<i>She has no computational abilities.</i>

00:08:00.542 --> 00:08:02.542
<i>That can't be right.</i>

00:08:04.917 --> 00:08:07.708
Whew, we're finally done.

00:08:07.708 --> 00:08:12.208
Good work. I'd sure
like something cool to drink.

00:08:12.208 --> 00:08:14.833
Ah, okay, I'll get it.

00:08:20.125 --> 00:08:22.833
Thank you very much, Sugata.

00:08:25.125 --> 00:08:27.292
It was an easy enough task.

00:08:27.292 --> 00:08:30.750
No, please allow us to
show our thanks somehow.

00:08:30.750 --> 00:08:32.917
We can't have you do this for nothing.

00:08:32.917 --> 00:08:35.917
I do expect something in return, of course.

00:08:39.417 --> 00:08:41.042
Look here.

00:08:42.333 --> 00:08:44.583
This is that thing from before.

00:08:44.583 --> 00:08:48.958
That geomagnetic disturbance
is still over our town.

00:08:48.958 --> 00:08:52.875
Up to now, the "New World"
had been circling the world,

00:08:52.875 --> 00:08:55.083
but now, it's holding position above our town.

00:08:55.083 --> 00:08:57.375
This has never happened before.

00:08:57.375 --> 00:09:00.875
I don't see anything up in the sky.

00:09:00.875 --> 00:09:03.125
Earlier, when I saw it,

00:09:03.125 --> 00:09:06.167
there was a gaping hole opened
up among the stars in the sky.

00:09:06.167 --> 00:09:09.750
Maybe it bends light around it in some way,

00:09:09.750 --> 00:09:12.250
or maybe it's hiding behind the clouds.

00:09:12.250 --> 00:09:14.042
Hey, Ikaros!

00:09:14.042 --> 00:09:16.333
Go fly around up there and have a look.

00:09:16.333 --> 00:09:17.958
Yes, Master.

00:09:36.458 --> 00:09:39.500
I did not see anything in particular.

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:42.958
Sugata, it really looks
like there's nothing there.

00:09:44.208 --> 00:09:46.375
<i>I knew it. She's...</i>

00:09:46.375 --> 00:09:48.958
Is something the matter, Sugata?

00:09:48.958 --> 00:09:51.833
Oh, no. It's all right.

00:09:51.833 --> 00:09:55.083
There's something that I want to check later,

00:09:55.083 --> 00:09:57.542
which I have to do myself.

00:09:59.917 --> 00:10:03.208
Sugata, are you planning to fly again?

00:10:04.625 --> 00:10:07.833
Yeah. I'm doing a trial flight tomorrow.

00:10:07.833 --> 00:10:10.958
I'd like to ask for your help with that.

00:10:10.958 --> 00:10:15.583
We've got tomorrow off,
and all, so you can stay over.

00:10:15.583 --> 00:10:16.792
Ready, set...

00:10:16.792 --> 00:10:18.042
...go!

00:10:18.042 --> 00:10:21.958
Okay then, Sugata
and I are in charge of cooking,

00:10:21.958 --> 00:10:25.208
Sakurai and Mitsuki,
you're in charge of fishing,

00:10:25.208 --> 00:10:27.792
and Ikaros is in charge of shopping.

00:10:27.792 --> 00:10:32.083
Ikaros shopping? No way,
she can't handle shopping!

00:10:32.083 --> 00:10:34.542
No, this could be a good opportunity.

00:10:34.542 --> 00:10:37.208
We should do various experiments to determine

00:10:37.208 --> 00:10:39.292
what kind of potential Ikaros has.

00:10:39.292 --> 00:10:43.250
Tomoki, you know almost nothing
of what Ikaros is capable of, right?

00:10:43.250 --> 00:10:45.833
Well, I guess not.

00:10:45.833 --> 00:10:48.750
We'll call it "Ikaros' First Errand."

00:10:48.750 --> 00:10:50.458
Sounds like fun!

00:10:50.458 --> 00:10:52.875
There you go, getting carried away again!

00:10:52.875 --> 00:10:57.583
It's all right. Everyone in this town is nice.

00:10:57.583 --> 00:11:00.458
I'm sure they'll help her.

00:11:02.125 --> 00:11:05.583
Okay, Ikaros, you go run our errand.

00:11:05.583 --> 00:11:08.708
And make sure you act like a normal person.

00:11:08.708 --> 00:11:10.333
Yes, Master.

00:11:12.375 --> 00:11:13.792
Wait!

00:11:14.375 --> 00:11:18.417
Get some money,
and ask what you have to buy first!

00:11:18.417 --> 00:11:20.375
Yes, Master.

00:11:21.417 --> 00:11:26.750
Here is a shopping list.
We're going to have curry tonight.

00:11:26.750 --> 00:11:29.000
All right, Master, off I go.

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:30.917
Hey!

00:11:30.917 --> 00:11:34.125
Do normal people go
flying off to run their errands?!

00:11:34.125 --> 00:11:34.792
Yes.

00:11:34.792 --> 00:11:36.333
Oh no they don't!

00:11:36.333 --> 00:11:37.542
Yes.

00:11:37.542 --> 00:11:39.875
"My First Errand"
"~Mysterious Creature Edition~"

00:11:40.208 --> 00:11:41.583
"Sorami Shopping District"

00:11:48.292 --> 00:11:51.208
"Watermelon ¥1200"

00:11:54.333 --> 00:11:56.792
"Watermelon ¥1200"

00:11:59.042 --> 00:12:00.458
Welcome!

00:12:02.292 --> 00:12:03.708
Miss...?

00:12:07.750 --> 00:12:10.417
If you like it that much,
I'll let you have it cheap.

00:12:10.417 --> 00:12:14.125
<i>I'm here because I'm worried.</i>
<i>What's she doing?</i>

00:12:14.125 --> 00:12:15.500
Hmm...

00:12:15.500 --> 00:12:16.333
--She seems to be drawn
to those watermelons.

00:12:16.333 --> 00:12:17.667
--Sugata?!
--She seems to be drawn to those watermelons.

00:12:17.667 --> 00:12:19.708
I was a little concerned about her, too.

00:12:19.708 --> 00:12:22.708
I wonder if she'll successfully
buy the ingredients for curry.

00:12:22.708 --> 00:12:25.708
Shh, she'll hear us.

00:12:25.708 --> 00:12:27.708
She's picking the vegetables.

00:12:27.708 --> 00:12:29.125
Carrots...

00:12:30.542 --> 00:12:32.042
Potatoes...

00:12:33.333 --> 00:12:34.542
Onions...

00:12:34.542 --> 00:12:35.333
"Konjac noodles"

00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:36.292
So close!

00:12:36.292 --> 00:12:37.042
--Not even close!

00:12:37.042 --> 00:12:38.250
--Thank you!
--Not even close!

00:12:38.250 --> 00:12:40.750
Looks like she ended up
getting a watermelon, too.

00:12:40.750 --> 00:12:43.042
A most interesting phenomenon.

00:12:47.333 --> 00:12:48.958
Next comes the meat.

00:12:48.958 --> 00:12:53.125
This will be the moment of truth.
It's the meat that makes the curry.

00:12:53.125 --> 00:12:56.250
Any curry without meat is no curry at all!

00:13:03.875 --> 00:13:05.292
Meat...

00:13:07.750 --> 00:13:10.292
Never mind! I don't need meat in my curry!

00:13:10.292 --> 00:13:13.083
I could clean a chick.

00:13:13.083 --> 00:13:14.583
No!!

00:13:15.167 --> 00:13:21.042
Watermelon... carrots...
potatoes... onions...

00:13:21.042 --> 00:13:22.625
meat...

00:13:23.208 --> 00:13:25.167
Chick curry, huh?

00:13:26.417 --> 00:13:29.875
No way! No way on earth!

00:13:29.875 --> 00:13:31.458
And also...

00:13:31.458 --> 00:13:33.292
...curry sauce.

00:13:33.292 --> 00:13:35.625
You can make curry out of that?

00:13:35.625 --> 00:13:39.250
Master, was my shopping good enough?

00:13:41.375 --> 00:13:45.167
You flunked.
You're gonna need more practice.

00:13:47.250 --> 00:13:49.083
I am sorry.

00:13:51.042 --> 00:13:55.333
Well, for your first time,
you did well. Nice going, Ikaros.

00:13:59.917 --> 00:14:04.125
"Heaven's Lost Property"

00:14:05.417 --> 00:14:09.042
Oh, Mom? I'll be all right.
Everyone else is here, too.

00:14:09.042 --> 00:14:11.667
Mm-hmm, all right. Thanks.

00:14:12.958 --> 00:14:15.542
I caught one! I caught one!

00:14:15.542 --> 00:14:17.542
--That's amazing, Tomo!
--Gotcha!

00:14:19.917 --> 00:14:22.625
Tomo, what do I do?!

00:14:26.375 --> 00:14:28.250
I'm soaked through.

00:14:37.083 --> 00:14:38.917
Hey, Tomoki...

00:14:38.917 --> 00:14:40.208
What?

00:14:40.208 --> 00:14:42.250
I can't seem to find Ikaros.

00:14:42.250 --> 00:14:45.958
Huh? Good grief...

00:14:45.958 --> 00:14:47.667
Where did she go?

00:14:47.667 --> 00:14:50.458
Hey, Ikaros!

00:14:50.458 --> 00:14:52.750
Wait, I hear something.

00:14:58.667 --> 00:14:59.750
W-What was that?!

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:02.000
A shockwave.

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:03.458
Here it comes again!

00:15:03.458 --> 00:15:04.875
Get down!

00:15:17.500 --> 00:15:19.500
What is that?!

00:15:19.500 --> 00:15:23.083
A pirarucu... The world's
largest freshwater fish,

00:15:23.083 --> 00:15:25.083
which lives in the Amazon river,
in South America.

00:15:25.083 --> 00:15:26.500
The Amazon?!

00:15:27.708 --> 00:15:30.625
How did you go all
the way to the Amazon?

00:15:30.625 --> 00:15:33.958
I am able to fly at Mach 24.

00:15:33.958 --> 00:15:34.542
--M-Mach?! You mean, you went around the earth?!

00:15:34.542 --> 00:15:38.792
--Mach 24 is roughly 30,000 kilometers per hour.
--M-Mach?! You mean, you went around the earth?!

00:15:38.792 --> 00:15:43.917
Well, since it's here,
let's clean it and have it for supper.

00:15:43.917 --> 00:15:46.625
I'm not sure we can eat that fish.

00:15:49.500 --> 00:15:52.958
What's the matter, Ei?
You look serious.

00:15:52.958 --> 00:15:54.792
Oh, Mikako...

00:15:54.792 --> 00:15:56.958
Are those Ikaros' specs?

00:15:56.958 --> 00:15:58.667
--Yeah. Her top speed is Mach--

00:15:58.667 --> 00:16:00.625
--Poor thing.
--Yeah. Her top speed is Mach--

00:16:01.667 --> 00:16:04.667
To be an angel, possessing abilities

00:16:04.667 --> 00:16:08.333
that not even our greatest
fighter planes have...

00:16:11.208 --> 00:16:13.958
"Pet-type" Angeloid, huh?

00:16:13.958 --> 00:16:15.833
Don't make me laugh.

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:18.833
Thank you for this dinner!

00:16:18.833 --> 00:16:21.667
Oh, it turned out to be
honest-to-goodness curry!

00:16:21.667 --> 00:16:24.083
Ikaros made it.

00:16:24.083 --> 00:16:28.375
You did? You really went
all-out, didn't you? Thanks.

00:16:34.458 --> 00:16:35.875
It's...

00:16:36.500 --> 00:16:39.125
<i>It reminds me of my mother's cooking.</i>

00:16:39.125 --> 00:16:40.833
<i>The sweetness is so...</i>

00:16:40.833 --> 00:16:42.917
Hey, this is meat and potatoes!

00:16:42.917 --> 00:16:45.125
You're right, it is sweet.

00:16:45.125 --> 00:16:49.750
Well, what does it matter?
Meat and potatoes is a lot like curry.

00:16:49.750 --> 00:16:52.042
They're not at all alike!

00:16:53.875 --> 00:16:55.542
What's with you, Sohara?

00:16:55.542 --> 00:16:59.500
Well, I mean,
this is starting to get funny.

00:16:59.500 --> 00:17:02.375
It seems like ever since Ikaros
arrived, things have been more fun.

00:17:02.375 --> 00:17:05.708
Yeah, I guess she didn't mean any harm, huh?

00:17:05.708 --> 00:17:11.125
Um, Master, why are you laughing?

00:17:11.125 --> 00:17:15.583
Why? Because we're having fun, of course.

00:17:15.583 --> 00:17:18.250
Fun?

00:17:18.250 --> 00:17:20.208
Fun...

00:17:25.042 --> 00:17:26.958
Nothing to report.

00:17:44.792 --> 00:17:46.500
What are you?

00:17:54.417 --> 00:17:56.708
I asked you what you are.

00:18:02.875 --> 00:18:06.417
I am a pet-type Angeloid, type Alpha...

00:18:06.417 --> 00:18:07.750
Don't play dumb.

00:18:07.750 --> 00:18:11.042
Would a pet-type need to be able
to catch a 5-meter fish alive,

00:18:11.042 --> 00:18:14.750
or fly at Mach 24?

00:18:14.750 --> 00:18:18.375
But then again,
your computational abilities are infantile,

00:18:18.375 --> 00:18:21.375
and your emotions appear
to be restricted, as well.

00:18:22.875 --> 00:18:26.917
Utterly perfect, yet utterly imperfect.

00:18:26.917 --> 00:18:29.083
What exactly are you?

00:18:32.167 --> 00:18:33.375
Answer me!

00:18:33.375 --> 00:18:36.667
For what purpose are
you sticking close to Tomoki?

00:18:39.333 --> 00:18:44.042
I am not sure what
my purpose should be.

00:18:44.042 --> 00:18:45.375
What?

00:18:45.375 --> 00:18:49.917
I was told by Master to stay at his side,

00:18:49.917 --> 00:18:52.875
so I can stay at his side,

00:18:52.875 --> 00:18:58.625
but it seems that every time I do
something, Master becomes angry.

00:19:00.958 --> 00:19:06.167
As Master's master has become angry,

00:19:06.167 --> 00:19:11.458
does this mean that
I ought not be at Master's side?

00:19:12.875 --> 00:19:17.167
<i>So she doesn't know what she is, herself?</i>

00:19:17.167 --> 00:19:22.750
<i>Then the question is,</i>
<i>who sent Ikaros to Tomoki?</i>

00:19:23.750 --> 00:19:25.667
Just enjoy yourself.

00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:29.833
Stay close to Tomoki, and enjoy yourself.

00:19:33.167 --> 00:19:37.833
All the while, praying the day never
comes when you must part ways.

00:19:47.083 --> 00:19:50.750
Wind, check! Position, check! Weather, check!

00:19:50.750 --> 00:19:52.167
Now, fly, Tomoki!

00:19:52.167 --> 00:19:54.750
Hold on! <i>You're </i>not flying, Sugata?!

00:19:56.000 --> 00:20:00.083
Experience is everything. Go get 'em!

00:20:00.083 --> 00:20:01.625
Takeoff!

00:20:01.625 --> 00:20:04.333
You fiend! You devil!

00:20:04.333 --> 00:20:07.208
Call me whatever you will,
this is for your homework.

00:20:07.208 --> 00:20:09.250
Tomo, hang in there!

00:20:09.250 --> 00:20:12.208
I give him two weeks until full recovery.

00:20:12.208 --> 00:20:14.833
My calculations are still coming up short.

00:20:14.833 --> 00:20:16.417
Um...

00:20:16.417 --> 00:20:18.417
May I ask you a question?

00:20:18.417 --> 00:20:19.750
What is it?

00:20:19.750 --> 00:20:25.875
Master's master, do you have fun being with Master?

00:20:27.083 --> 00:20:32.875
I still do not entirely understand
the meaning of the word "fun."

00:20:32.875 --> 00:20:33.875
I just...

00:20:33.875 --> 00:20:35.500
Just what?

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:38.417
When I am with Master...

00:20:40.083 --> 00:20:45.625
How can I put it?
My heart just seems to feel lighter.

00:20:45.625 --> 00:20:47.625
Hmm, I see.

00:20:50.583 --> 00:20:52.750
Let's make this your homework.

00:20:52.750 --> 00:20:55.917
Turn in a report to me sometime.

00:20:55.917 --> 00:20:57.208
Yes.

00:20:58.667 --> 00:21:00.292
We're home!

00:21:02.292 --> 00:21:03.625
I'm exhausted.

00:21:03.625 --> 00:21:06.542
Tomo, it's lucky for you
that you weren't seriously hurt.

00:21:11.333 --> 00:21:13.583
You brought the watermelon home with you?

00:21:13.583 --> 00:21:14.250
--Yes.

00:21:14.250 --> 00:21:17.292
--Well then, let's eat it right away.
--Yes.

00:21:18.542 --> 00:21:21.375
You've really taken a liking to it, huh?

00:21:26.167 --> 00:21:28.042
At any rate, our homework is done.

00:21:28.042 --> 00:21:33.833
And say what you will,
that was fun, like we went camping, huh?

00:21:35.292 --> 00:21:38.917
Yeah, you're right.
Looking back at it now, that was funny.

00:21:38.917 --> 00:21:43.125
Master, is it fun to be with me?

00:21:43.125 --> 00:21:48.708
Yeah, it's fun. All sorts of things
happen, and it never gets dull.

00:21:50.083 --> 00:21:52.458
This item is now up for sale!

00:21:55.583 --> 00:21:57.958
What are you doing, Ikaros?

00:21:57.958 --> 00:21:59.958
This is my homework.

00:22:01.750 --> 00:22:05.125
"Ikaros + Master = fun"

00:22:17.125 --> 00:22:23.583
<i>What are you gazing at right now,</i>

00:22:23.583 --> 00:22:30.333
<i>your eyes moist with youthful woe?</i>

00:22:30.333 --> 00:22:42.750
<i>Is it a fleeing white dove, or is it love?</i>

00:22:42.750 --> 00:22:49.542
<i>As of today, you are one of us</i>

00:22:49.542 --> 00:22:56.833
<i>Let's fly away under blue skies</i>

00:23:03.917 --> 00:23:16.292
<i>Youth is a season given by the sun</i>

00:23:16.292 --> 00:23:23.083
<i>As of today, you are one of us</i>

00:23:23.083 --> 00:23:29.500
<i>Let's set these once-in-a-lifetime days ablaze</i>

00:23:29.500 --> 00:23:36.500
<i>Let's set these once-in-a-lifetime days ablaze</i>

00:23:50.208 --> 00:23:52.250
Has this thing come loose?

00:23:59.708 --> 00:24:02.708
Don't use that to play with!

00:24:03.792 --> 00:24:08.086
Next time,
"Love and Triangles, Revisited"
